  "_conventions": "SI internally, mm/deg on every interface with the unit as a key suffix. Z is the axis of revolution and the gas flows +Z (in reverse_annular the GAS turns 180 deg twice, but the geometric axis is still Z). liner.profile rows are [z_mm, r_inner_mm, r_outer_mm]; casing.profile rows are [z_mm, r_mm] with r the INNER radius. hole_rows[].angle_deg is the tilt of the hole AXIS away from the RADIAL direction towards +Z (0 = purely radial, 90 = purely axial); an explicit `axis` = [radial, tangential, axial] wins over it. effusion.angle_deg is measured from the liner SURFACE, not from the normal. g <= 0 means feasible.",
